[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked **known**: one bug, one fix queued. It is not one bug. Read
the reports by where they came in and what they say, and #4471 holds three problems. The queued
parser fix closes only the first. Each problem now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not known. Three problems, one fix queued. The other two stay open until they have their own fixes.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** A tenant whose locale writes the
day first gets day and month swapped: 2 March comes out as 3 February. Every channel of every
booking-v2 tenant, and the app and email of booking-v3 tenants. This is the bug #4471 names, and
the queued fix is for it.

**`hint`: booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field.** The tenant's people type
what the hint tells them, month first, and the form then reads the date the tenant's way, day
first. The parser fix does not touch this: the hint must match the tenant's locale (or the form
must read what it asks for). Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants.

**`one-day`: the date moves by exactly one day.** No month is swapped. Tuesday shows as Monday,
an invite arrives before the booking was made, and two clients in different time zones get two
different days for the same meeting. That is a time zone bug: a date-only value turned into an
instant and back. The desk already noted these reports (`desk-notes.json` → `oneDayMove`) but
counted them under `parser` because of their tenant. The parser fix will not move them back.

## Why one ticket held three

Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line alone. The
subject says how someone noticed, not what broke, so the same subjects turn up across problems:

<SubjectSpread ticket={4471} />

Intake's own tag (`meta.intakeTag`) does not help either: it follows the browser's locale, not the
tenant's form, so it marks every report sent from an `en-US` browser as `hint`, whatever way
it came in, and misses booking-v3 form reports sent from day-first browsers.

## How the counts are made

- Numbers on this page come from `#lib/kb/split` at render time, over the export in
  `src/lib/data`. When the desk merges more reports or adds to its notes, rebuild and the page follows.
- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, so repeated ids count once.
- A report is `one-day` when the desk's notes list it; otherwise its cause comes from
  `causes.ts` (tenant locale, booking form, channel). A report with no tenant on file would show as
  `unplaced`.

## Next

- Decision 0001 should be replaced by a new record: merge by cause, not by subject.
- Re-check this page against a fresh export before closing any of the three tickets.

